        "answer": {
          "short": "$A\\cup B\\cup C$",
          "worked": "Taking the complement changes an intersection to a union of complements. Taking a complement twice returns the original set.\n$$\\begin{align*}(A'\\cap B'\\cap C')'&=A''\\cup B''\\cup C''\\\\(A'\\cap B'\\cap C')'&=A\\cup B\\cup C.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
